    "q-126325": {
      "dom_id": "step-q126325",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14224622/assets/b61c628a012f6bde3144254b521e11f8803e089cd7f83f2c19a1255cf22c0e3a.png)\n\nConsider the finite region bounded by the curves $x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}},$ $x=-\\frac{1}{2}y+1,$ and the $x$-axis, as shown above. Find an integral expression for the volume of the solid generated when this region is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let $f(y)=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}$ and $g(y)=-\\frac{1}{2}y+1.$\n\nWe start by determining the points where the curves intersect by solving the following equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y) & =g(y) \\\\ \\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}} & =-\\frac{1}{2}y+1 \\\\ 4-{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{2}-y+1 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{4}{y}^{2}+y+3 & =0 \\\\ 5{y}^{2}-4y-12 & =0 \\\\ (5y+6)(y-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution corresponding to our region is $y=2.$ So, we need to integrate from $y=0$ to $y=2.$ \n\nNow, let's draw our usual horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left and right functions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14224622/assets/122a21e72dc7473cc34ed3ece0325294eadcc86cbe8a5b91e4dfe4be77b369c0.png)\n\nThe horizontal arrow \n\n- *enters* the region through the left function $x=g(y)=-\\frac{1}{2}y+1,$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the right function $x=f(y)=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}.$\n\nTherefore, using the shell method, the volume of the solid can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =2\\pi {\\int }_{c}^{d}y([\\text{right}]-[\\text{left}])\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}y([\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}]-[-\\frac{1}{2}y+1])\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}y(\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2}y-1)\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-126325-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}y(\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2}y+1)\\text{d}y",
              "html": "  <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"50\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D70B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mstyle><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-msubsup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-lop\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c222B TEX-S2\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.896em; margin-left: -0.388em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\" style=\"margin-left: 0.647em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom><mjx-spacer style=\"margin-top: 1.513em;\"></mjx-spacer><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msubsup><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mrow space=\"2\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-s3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28 TEX-S3\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-msqrt><mjx-sqrt><mjx-surd><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-sop\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c221A TEX-S1\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-surd><mjx-box style=\"padding-top: 0.173em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-msup space=\"3\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.289em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msup></mjx-box></mjx-sqrt></mjx-msqrt><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle space=\"3\"><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></m